<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Apuani</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Apuani were a Ligurian people of the mountains of north-western Tuscany, between the Magra and Serchio valleys, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apuan-alps">Apuan Alps</a> keep their name. They resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> stubbornly in the early 2nd century BCE until, in 180 BCE, the consuls deported about 40,000 of them with their families to Samnium in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, where they became the Ligures Baebiani and Corneliani.</p></div>
